; hark: root-hints = 127.0.10.1
; hark: dnssec-zone = .

SCENARIO_BEGIN aggressive NSEC synthesises NXDOMAIN for sibling in cached range (RFC 8198)

; End-to-end coverage for `src/nsec_cache.zig`. The module has 15 unit
; tests but no scenario asserting the synthesis path fires on a real
; recursive resolution.
;
; Zone layout (signed root, harness-generated key):
;   `.`  — apex (SOA + NS + DNSKEY)
;   `a.` — A record
;   `c.` — A record
;
; Canonical owner ordering (RFC 4034 §6.1, octet-wise with absent < 0):
;   . < a. < b. < b2. < c.
;
; Step 1 primes the cache with a live query for `b. A`. The responder
; returns NXDOMAIN with two NSEC proofs:
;   1. `a. NSEC c.` covers every name strictly between `a.` and `c.`,
;      including both `b.` and `b2.`.
;   2. `. NSEC a.` covers `*.` (0x2A `*` < 0x61 `a`), proving no
;      wildcard would have matched.
; Both get validated against the harness-signed DNSKEY for `.` and
; stored in the aggressive NSEC cache.
;
; Step 3 queries `b2. A`. The scenario declares ONLY ONE upstream entry
; (for `b.`). If hark goes upstream for `b2.`, the responder returns
; REFUSED (responder.py:244, default for unmatched queries), hark
; surfaces SERVFAIL, and step 4's `MATCH flags … AD NXDOMAIN` fails.
;
; The only path that produces NXDOMAIN with AD=1 for `b2.` without an
; upstream query is RFC 8198 §5.3 synthesis from cached NSEC records.

RANGE_BEGIN 0 100
  ADDRESS 127.0.10.1

  ENTRY_BEGIN
    MATCH opcode qname qtype
    ADJUST copy_id copy_query
    REPLY QR AA NXDOMAIN
    SECTION QUESTION
      b. IN A
    SECTION AUTHORITY
      . 3600 IN SOA root. nobody.invalid. 1 7200 3600 86400 3600
      . 3600 IN NSEC a. SOA NS DNSKEY RRSIG NSEC
      a. 3600 IN NSEC c. A RRSIG NSEC
  ENTRY_END
RANGE_END

STEP 1 QUERY
ENTRY_BEGIN
  REPLY RD DO
  SECTION QUESTION
    b. IN A
ENTRY_END

STEP 2 CHECK_ANSWER
ENTRY_BEGIN
  MATCH flags question
  REPLY QR RD RA AD NXDOMAIN
  SECTION QUESTION
    b. IN A
ENTRY_END

STEP 3 QUERY
ENTRY_BEGIN
  REPLY RD DO
  SECTION QUESTION
    b2. IN A
ENTRY_END

STEP 4 CHECK_ANSWER
ENTRY_BEGIN
  MATCH flags question
  REPLY QR RD RA AD NXDOMAIN
  SECTION QUESTION
    b2. IN A
ENTRY_END

SCENARIO_END
